WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:02.960 --> 00:00:04.280
What is a line?

00:00:04.420 --> 00:00:06.880
It is basically a thin straight mark

00:00:06.880 --> 00:00:09.000
made by a pencil or a marker

00:00:09.200 --> 00:00:12.600
and it extends indefinitely in both directions.

00:00:12.820 --> 00:00:16.640
But I can also draw a line like this or like this.

00:00:16.880 --> 00:00:21.600
It means that we do not have a single way in which a line can be drawn.

00:00:21.900 --> 00:00:24.160
We just draw a part of a line.

00:00:24.540 --> 00:00:27.780
Lines are generally named with lowercase letters.

00:00:28.020 --> 00:00:30.120
This can be called line 'p',

00:00:30.400 --> 00:00:35.220
or we can draw a line like this and mark two points 'A and B'.

00:00:35.700 --> 00:00:38.200
This will be called line 'AB'.

00:00:38.460 --> 00:00:45.520
Line 'AB' can also be written as 'AB' with a tiny line drawn over 'AB'.

00:00:45.660 --> 00:00:47.200
So what is a ray?

00:00:47.440 --> 00:00:52.660
A ray starts at one point and goes on indefinitely in one direction.

00:00:52.960 --> 00:00:56.920
Just like for lines even rays can be drawn in different ways.

00:00:57.080 --> 00:01:00.560
What we draw is just a part of a ray.

00:01:00.800 --> 00:01:02.720
We can mark this point as 'A',

00:01:02.720 --> 00:01:05.380
and mark a point 'B' somewhere on the ray!

00:01:05.720 --> 00:01:08.080
We can call this ray 'AB'.

00:01:08.520 --> 00:01:12.200
Or write 'AB' with a tiny ray over it.

00:01:12.500 --> 00:01:15.040
This tells us that the ray starts at point 'A'.

00:01:15.260 --> 00:01:18.460
and goes indefinitely in one direction.

00:01:18.840 --> 00:01:20.540
It's a bit ironical.

00:01:20.720 --> 00:01:25.300
But the point at which the rate begins is called the end point of the Ray.

00:01:25.460 --> 00:01:28.340
Here, 'A' is the end point of this ray!

00:01:28.400 --> 00:01:31.180
Which means it cannot be written as ray 'BA'.

00:01:31.500 --> 00:01:34.500
Or 'BA' with a tiny ray over it.

00:01:34.740 --> 00:01:38.480
But line 'AB' can also be written as line 'BA'.

00:01:38.740 --> 00:01:42.280
We just need to be careful when we are dealing with a ray.

00:01:42.500 --> 00:01:46.300
Now let's get to the final concept in this video.

00:01:46.580 --> 00:01:48.620
Look at what we have drawn here.

00:01:48.900 --> 00:01:51.420
We can see that it has two end points.

00:01:51.800 --> 00:01:56.140
This is called a line segment, and it is a fixed part of a line.

00:01:56.440 --> 00:01:58.520
This is its specified length,

00:01:58.560 --> 00:02:02.960
and it does not extend indefinitely in any direction.

00:02:03.100 --> 00:02:08.320
If the end points are 'A' and 'B'. This can be called line segment 'AB'.

00:02:08.580 --> 00:02:13.100
Or it can also be written as 'AB' with a line segment over it.

00:02:13.460 --> 00:02:18.980
And yes, we can also write this as 'BA' with a line segment over it.

00:02:19.200 --> 00:02:22.680
A line extends indefinitely in both directions.

00:02:23.120 --> 00:02:25.240
A ray starts at its end point .

00:02:25.380 --> 00:02:28.100
And goes indefinitely in one direction .

00:02:28.380 --> 00:02:31.880
And a line segment is a fixed part of a line.

